  "body": "## Problem\n\nSiemens, *SINUMERIK ONE / 840D sl / 828D ISO dialects*, Function Manual, 07/2021, section 6.3, table 6-2 (drilling cycles, ISO dialect M) gives the address words of each cycle. Two cycles in `assets/posts/sinumerik.cps` (`onCycle()`) do not agree with it:\n\n- G84 (tapping): the table lists a P word. The post drops a G84 dwell and gives no warning (`g !== \"G84\"`).\n- G85 (ream, `REAM`): the table lists no P word. The post writes `P<ms>` on G85 when the dwell is above 0.\n\nThe G86 dwell refusal agrees with the table (no P on G86). G82 and G89 agree (P listed).\n\n## Expected\n\n- G84: the post writes the P dwell, or it refuses the dwell by name with `msg()`. It never drops it silently.\n- G85: the post refuses a dwell by name, or it gives a source that shows P on G85.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Do not change behaviour without a source. Use behaviour only from the manual; do not copy its text.\n- Check first if the stream can give a TAP or REAM cycle with a dwell above 0.\n- Found during #2349 / PR #2353.\n",
